respective  manual pages may be consulted), the following general
variables are  defined:  Boolean:  enable/disable  forwarding  of
packets.   Also, identify if the node is acting as a router.  De‐
faults to off.  Boolean: enable/disable sending of  redirects  in
response to unforwardable packets.  This option is ignored unless
the  node  is  routing packets, and should normally be enabled on
all systems.  Defaults to on.  Integer: default hop  limit  value
to  use  for  outgoing  packets.   This  value applies to all the
transport protocols on top of There  are  APIs  to  override  the
value.  Integer: default maximum number of fragmented packets the
node  will  accept.   0  means  that the node will not accept any
fragmented packets.  ‐1 means that the node will accept  as  many
fragmented  packets  as  it receives.  The flag is provided basi‐
cally for avoiding possible DoS attacks.  Boolean: enable/disable
receiving of router advertisement packets, and  autoconfiguration
of address prefixes and default routers.  The node must be a host
(not a router) for the option to be meaningful.  Defaults to off.
